WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.630
- Listen, I'll be honest with you,

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.490
I'm emotional about it as well

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.740
because it is 100% my
biggest vulnerability too.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.320
It might be at different scales,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.150
people may look at like all this,

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.920
but I've left so much on the table.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.640
Like I own nothing of Wine Library.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.220
AJ owned 50% of this when
I had all the leverage.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.490
Like, I've left so much and
my great fear is resentment.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.662
- [Guy] Right, and that's what
I keep telling her is that,

00:00:51.662 --> 00:00:53.470
here's the thing, I don't wanna look back,

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.934
it's give and then at
some point down the road

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:58.230
success meets opportunity, right.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.160
It's one of those things
where I've planned,

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.230
even for like this moment,
I've shot hundreds of vlogs

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.440
hundreds of times, built all
these things and it's like,

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.910
you don't know when that
one time, that one--

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.740
- 'Cause I don't think
it's one time, to be frank.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.830
My intuition is it's
getting into the pattern

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.510
of asking for what you're looking for

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.340
but being okay with not getting it.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.790
- Right.
- Patience.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:24.230
- [Guy] And making the video
content and nobody watches--

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:25.870
- And when you give,

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:29.140
giving means you have no
expectation on the other side.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.650
Manipulating is when you give

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.489
with the thought you're gonna get.

00:01:32.489 --> 00:01:36.090
And what people that love people that give

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:41.090
don't understand is it's
our natural DNA, the end.

00:01:42.981 --> 00:01:46.010
- But as a wife she's going,
I just wanna see you win.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.230
- But winning comes in a
lot of shapes and forms.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.360
I'll be very frank with you,

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.320
if I do not buy the New York Jets

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.150
I would've won because
winning for me is the chase

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.313
of the New York Jets.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.340
I've already won.
- You always say, the journey.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.350
- 100%, like people don't wanna hear it,

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.970
I'll get booed when I'm
90 for not doing it.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.480
- But do you care?
- Of course not

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.210
because that's winning for me and winning,

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:09.660
you know, spouses especially,
is a real tricky one,

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.330
it's of all the ones
it's the trickiest one

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.620
because they love you the most

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.283
and they're most tied into you.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:18.500
So I have a lot of empathy
for the men and women

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.749
who have a spouse who's on the give train.

00:02:21.749 --> 00:02:23.800
You know, you have to define winning,

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.950
if you've been giving this whole time

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.360
with the hope that some shoe drops

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.070
I have a ton of empathy for that

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:31.760
but you have to frame that in your head.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.901
- [Guy] I think I give
because I wanna help people.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.903
I'm a lot like you.
- Well then you've won.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.450
But you have to ask
yourself, and it's okay

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.320
if you've been hoping that it leads,

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.260
that's unbelievably okay,

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.730
just as okay as somebody who always takes,

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.490
everything's okay.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:48.760
You first have to ask
yourself, which one is it?

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:53.460
For me I will never let
anybody have leverage on me,

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.230
that is my happiness.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.816
- [Guy] Well it's like
creating YouTube content

00:02:56.816 --> 00:03:00.577
and then I don't really, I
create content to help and give

00:03:00.577 --> 00:03:02.950
and don't make content to cave

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.812
to what other's expectations are.

00:03:04.812 --> 00:03:07.383
- I get it, I get it.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:13.330
I think deciding what winning
is is the most important part.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.050
If you're hope is that all this giving

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:17.938
leads to business
opportunities, that's great.

00:03:17.938 --> 00:03:20.070
I wrote a book called
Jab, Jab, Jab, Right Hook.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.610
I believe that that's how it does work,

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.530
but only in the macro.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.840
I will never give to
her with the expectation

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.530
that she delivers for
me of something I need.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.790
I'll be comfortable to ask,

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.210
I won't be disappointed if, like I've had,

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.450
I've told some stories,
unbelievable, I've given,

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:42.651
asked for something a tenth
of it, person didn't deliver.

00:03:42.651 --> 00:03:44.870
You know, look, there's that initial,

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.946
like, fuck, and then you're like,

00:03:46.946 --> 00:03:50.210
I don't have the capability of dwelling.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.630
So I think the question becomes
for you, what is winning?

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:57.990
For me, no question, I'm about statues

00:03:57.990 --> 00:03:59.750
and how many people show up to my funeral.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.160
It's very clear to me.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.300
- [Guy] I'll be there.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.660
- And so to me, that matters.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.270
Like, I wanna stun my grandkids

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.760
of how many people decided to show up.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:11.860
The greatest day of my life

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.710
will be the first day I don't see it.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.130
You know, I know that.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:20.383
And so as you can imagine,
just giving is that leverage.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:24.500
But if you're looking for some
short term financial reward

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:25.660
that's super acceptable,

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.040
what you need to make the change of then

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.380
is being clear about that,

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:32.020
because the cliche thing
I see in other givers

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.880
is they love the altruism that they give

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.110
but they have a burning
resentment and anger

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:38.469
or fear inside that they're not getting.

00:04:38.469 --> 00:04:41.630
- [Guy] It's not that, it's I
kinda feel guilty to ask for

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.960
the monetary value, does this make sense?

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.618
- Of course, I'll tell you why.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.880
'Cause you didn't ask for it up front

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.643
or set the framework for the
potential of it up front.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:53.430
Which makes sense, right?
- Right.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.650
- You see where I'm going?

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.400
That makes sense, because
if you didn't do it

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.840
now you know you're sandbagging the person

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.520
and that makes you feel bad, as it should.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.553
I love that about you, on a quick read.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.760
What you wanna think about
is is that macro work

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.210
leading to opportunity 'cause
somebody's word of mouth

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:10.110
or do you set it up in
the beginning and be like,

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.130
hey brother, I'll give you one video

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:14.200
but then I want you to buy
one video and that's great,

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.120
and would you like that or
no, and that's up to you.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.500
- [Guy] And I have never done that,

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.043
I've just instantly given.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:23.290
- And by the way, you've
gotten without even knowing

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.830
for that giving in many different ways.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:29.500
The question becomes,
A, what's the difference

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:34.213
between you winning from your
eyes versus your wife's eyes,

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.930
but it starts with you
because your wife is taking

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:42.600
pillow talk and random
conversations and making it her own,

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.281
I know I gotta go, right?

00:05:44.281 --> 00:05:46.500
You know what I mean, super important.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.809
And here's the best part about 49,

00:05:48.809 --> 00:05:51.280
you're at fuckin' half time.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.230
And it's really hard to know that

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:56.030
because when you're 22 49 feels finished.

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:58.922
But when you're, think
about how young we all feel.

00:05:58.922 --> 00:05:59.755
- [Guy] And I feel great.

00:05:59.755 --> 00:06:01.880
- I wish he knew that
we feel the same as him.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.980
Hold old are you, Jas, how old are you?

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:05.540
- [Jason] 23, uh four.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:07.390
- Oh right, turned a couple days ago.

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:11.150
What 24 doesn't know is
when you're double the age

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:14.520
you feel exactly the same
inside, exactly the same.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.890
You guys feel exactly the fuckin' same.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.157
- [Guy] I still have
the same insecurities--

00:06:19.157 --> 00:06:21.337
- That's right, it's the
same fuckin' everything.

00:06:21.337 --> 00:06:22.920
- [Guy] Right, and here I am,
people ask me what do you do,

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.390
and I was like, I make videos

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:26.755
and I'm a YouTuber at 49 years old,

00:06:26.755 --> 00:06:27.880
it's scary as hell sometimes.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.680
- Yeah.
- It's fun.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.453
- Just gotta ask, up front.

00:06:33.433 --> 00:06:34.390
- [Guy] I do appreciate that.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:37.760
- You know what I mean, I'm
